[6] VERDICT
    (i)   exact submultiplicativity: REFUTED [T]  (a_1=1; worst violation 34.41)
    (ii)  sequence is empirically SUPERmultiplicative on all 9 pairs tested [E]
    (iii) Fekete(super) => lambda* = sup_n a_n^(1/n) = lim exists;
          finite terms give LOWER bounds only: lambda* >= a_6^(1/6) = 13.901997
    (iv)  Fekete(sub or C-form) would give UPPER bounds; neither hypothesis holds:
          sub is false; uniform C is unproven (and observed C >= 34.41 is rising).
    (v)   => (b): finitely many terms + Fekete CANNOT prove lambda* <= 48.
          lambda*<=48 needs a uniform-glue lemma  a_(m+n) <= 1694 a_m a_n  [C],
          or a local ratio lemma a_(n+1) <= B a_n with B<=48 [T]-level bookkeeping.
    (vi)  more terms (n=7..12) would only raise the LOWER bound (to ~26-30);
          they can never yield an upper bound. No finite n suffices.
